itle = 'Leave'\r\n  notes = 'It is time to leave.'\r\n  location = ''\r\n\r\n  # Create the reminder event\r\n  computer.calendar.create_event(title=title, start_date=reminder_date_time, notes=notes, location=location)\r\n\r\n\r\n  Would you like to run this code? (y/n)\r\n\r\n  y\r\n\r\n\r\n  title = 'Leave'\r\n  notes = 'It is time to leave.'\r\n  location = ''\r\n\r\n  # Create the reminder event\r\n  computer.calendar.create_event(title=title, start_date=reminder_date_time, notes=notes, location=location)\r\n\r\n\r\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  TypeError                                 Traceback (most recent call last)\r\n  Cell In[18], line 12\r\n       10 pass\r\n       11 print('##active_line6##')\r\n  ---> 12 computer.calendar.create_event(title=title, start_date=reminder_date_time, notes=notes, location=location)\r\n\r\n  TypeError: Calendar.create_event() missing 1 required positional argument: 'end_date'\r\n\r\n\r\n  I apologize for the oversight. The error indicates that the 'end_date' argument is indeed necessary for the 'create_event' function.\r\n\r\n  Let's solve this by adding 10 minutes to the reminder_date_time to establish a range for the event.\r\n\r\n  Let's execute this in the next step.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  end_date = reminder_date_time + datetime.timedelta(minutes=5)\r\n\r\n  # Create the reminder event\r\n  computer.calendar.create_event(title=title, start_date=reminder_date_time, end_date=end_date, notes=notes, location=location)\r\n\r\n\r\n  Would you like to run this code? (y/n)\r\n\r\n  y\r\n\r\n\r\n  end_date = reminder_date_time + datetime.timedelta(minutes=5)\r\n\r\n\r\n  end_date = reminder_date_time + datetime.timedelta(minutes=5)\r\n\r\n  # Create the reminder event\r\n  computer.calendar.create_event(title=title, start_date=reminder_date_time, end_date=end_date, notes=notes, location=location)\r\n\r\n\r\n  Output truncated. Showing the last 2800 characters.\r\n\r\n  first calendar